---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { LOGO_VIEWBOX, LOGO_INNER_TRANSFORM, CHAIR_PATH, ORB_PATH } from "../../lib/logoPaths.js";
---
<Base
  title="Teardown Questionnaire | No Empty Chair"
  description="The full deep-dive questionnaire for your $200 Teardown, plus how to get me temporary access to your site and accounts."
  canonical="https://noemptychair.co/teardown/questionnaire"
  noindex={true}>
  <main id="main" class="disc-page">
    <header class="tp-head">
      <a href="/" class="tp-logo">No Empty <span>Chair</span></a>
    </header>

    <div class="tp-wrap disc-wrap">
      <div class="tp-mark">
        <svg width="40" height="50.5" viewBox={LOGO_VIEWBOX} preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" role="img" aria-label="No Empty Chair mark">
          <g fill="#413645" stroke="none"><g transform={LOGO_INNER_TRANSFORM}><path d={CHAIR_PATH} /></g></g>
          <g transform={LOGO_INNER_TRANSFORM}><path d={ORB_PATH} fill="#a85a76" /></g>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-intro">
        <div class="disc-kick">$200 Teardown <span class="disc-free">Step 3 of 4</span></div>
        <h1>You're in. Here's what's next.</h1>
        <p>Thanks for taking care of the $200. You won't find a worksheet here, I pull your numbers myself once I'm in. Just two things below: what I'm actually looking at, and how to get me access.</p>
      </div>

      <form
        class="tform disc-form"
        name="teardown-questionnaire"
        method="POST"
        data-netlify="true"
        netlify-honeypot="bot-field"
        action="/teardown-questionnaire-thanks"
      >
        <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="teardown-questionnaire" />
        <input class="tp-hp" aria-hidden="true" type="text" name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />

        <label>Who's filling this out?
          <select name="filled_by">
            <option value="client">I'm filling this out myself</option>
            <option value="makayla">Makayla's filling this out with me (call or in person)</option>
          </select>
        </label>

        <div class="disc-sec">
          <div class="disc-sec-h"><span class="disc-num">1</span>Confirm It's You</div>
          <div class="tp-row">
            <label>Your name<input required type="text" name="name" placeholder="First & last" /></label>
            <label>Salon / business name<input required type="text" name="salon" placeholder="Same as your first form" /></label>
          </div>
          <label>Best email<input required type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@email.com" /></label>
        </div>

        <div class="disc-sec">
          <div class="disc-sec-h"><span class="disc-num">2</span>What I'm Pulling, and What It Means</div>
          <ul class="otc-pull">
            <li><b>Your numbers</b> (followers, reach, views over the last 30/60/90 days) — tells me whether your content is actually reaching people, or just sitting there.</li>
            <li><b>Your current content and voice</b> — tells me what's already working, what's inconsistent, and where the brand feels unclear.</li>
            <li><b>Your booking flow</b> — tells me exactly where people drop off before they book.</li>
            <li><b>Your site and profile setup</b> — tells me what's quietly costing you visibility: SEO, bio links, contact info, load speed.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="tp-fine" style="text-align:left;margin:10px 0 0">None of it needs a form from you, just the access below.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="disc-sec">
          <div class="disc-sec-h"><span class="disc-num">3</span>Temporary Access</div>
          <p class="tp-fine" style="text-align:left;margin:0 0 14px">To actually click through everything myself, I need temporary access to your site and main social accounts for 48 to 72 hours. Add <b>hello@noemptychair.co</b> as a collaborator wherever that's possible: Instagram under Settings → Business tools → Collaborators (or just share a login if it's a personal account), Facebook as a Page partner, and your website as an admin, editor, or staff account on whatever it's built on. Pull my access once the teardown's done, totally fine.</p>
          <div class="otc-tip">Don't want to hand over an actual password? Set up a shared vault in a password manager (1Password and Bitwarden both do this) and share it there instead, it's safer than texting a password and you can revoke it in one click when we're done.</div>
          <label>What's your website built on?
            <select name="platform">
              <option value="">Choose one…</option>
              <option>Wix</option>
              <option>Squarespace</option>
              <option>Shopify</option>
              <option>WordPress</option>
              <option>Something else</option>
              <option>Don't have a site yet</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label style="margin-top:14px">Anything about getting me access I should know?
            <span class="hint">Optional. A heads up on who to loop in, a site that's not live yet, whatever's worth flagging.</span>
            <textarea name="access_notes" rows="3"></textarea>
          </label>
        </div>

        <button class="btn" type="submit">Send it over →</button>
        <p class="tp-fine">Goes straight to me, I'll confirm I've got it and get started.</p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </main>
  <style>
    .disc-free{display:inline-block;margin-left:8px;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:100px;background:rgba(168,90,118,.12);color:#a85a76;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;vertical-align:middle;}
    .otc-pull{margin:0;padding-left:20px;display:grid;gap:10px;}
    .otc-pull li{font-size:14px;color:#4b4149;line-height:1.5;}
    .otc-pull b{color:#2a232e;}
    .otc-tip{margin:0 0 16px;padding:12px 14px;background:rgba(168,90,118,.08);border:1px solid rgba(168,90,118,.25);border-radius:10px;font-size:13px;color:#4b4149;line-height:1.5;}
  </style>
  <script is:inline>
    /* Pre-fill from the link's query string (?name=...&salon=...&email=...) so
       a client's basics from an earlier step don't have to be retyped here. */
    (function () {
      try {
        var params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
        var map = { name: ["name"], salon: ["salon", "business_name", "business"], email: ["email"] };
        var form = document.querySelector('form[name="teardown-questionnaire"]:not([hidden])');
        if (!form) return;
        Object.keys(map).forEach(function (field) {
          var input = form.querySelector('[name="' + field + '"]');
          if (!input || input.value) return;
          for (var i = 0; i < map[field].length; i++) {
            var v = params.get(map[field][i]);
            if (v) { input.value = v; break; }
          }
        });
      } catch (e) {}
    })();
  </script>
  <script is:inline>
    /* Backup notifier: on submit, also POST to a function that emails you directly,
       so a spam-flagged Netlify submission never means a silently missed lead.
       Fire-and-forget — the native Netlify submission still proceeds normally. */
    (function () {
      var f = document.querySelector('form[name="teardown-questionnaire"]:not([hidden])');
      if (!f) return;
      f.addEventListener("submit", function () {
        try {
          var data = { _form: "teardown-questionnaire" };
          new FormData(f).forEach(function (v, k) {
            if (k === "bot-field" || k === "form-name") return;
            if (data[k] !== undefined) data[k] = [].concat(data[k], v);
            else data[k] = v;
          });
          fetch("/.netlify/functions/lead-notify", {
            method: "POST",
            headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
            body: JSON.stringify(data),
            keepalive: true,
          }).catch(function () {});
        } catch (e) {}
        /* no preventDefault — let Netlify capture it too */
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
